    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d410">

                <pb facs="0481" n="471" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg471"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5151/967</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Financial Division</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Livesey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Berle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-10-11">October 11, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Berle</hi>: These papers<anchor n="90"
                        xml:id="d410-f1"/> show the present status of the China Stabilization
                    Agreement renewal with revision proposal, which has been lost to sight for some
                    weeks. Treasury proposes to stall indefinitely.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d410-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d410-f1" n="90" xml:id="d410-f1-content">
                <p>See memoranda of October 6 and 7, <ref target="#pg468">pp. 468</ref> and <ref
                        target="#pg470">470</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d410-f2" n="91" xml:id="d410-f2-content">
                <p>Notation by Mr. Berle: “Unless you see some reason to the contrary, FE’s memo
                    seems sound.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
